# `b: Box<Pt>` binds Pt and calls `gx$Pt`, exactly as `gx<Pt>(b)` does. Anything else infers i64
# — today's base, and its refusal. A scalar other than i64 (`b: Box<i32>`) marks `_gi_sc`, so the
# call instantiates `gx$i32` as `gx<i32>(b)` does (its base takes a `Box`: a different layout).
# `mth` 1: a method call, whose list starts at parameter 1 (`_mcall_infer`, 6.7.11). CHANGELOG [6.7.8]
# ⛔ 6.7.16 — a `**G<..T..>` carrier (bit 9, `_gs_pparam`) reads its whole argument through its pointers, as a
# `pp: **T` does (`_ic_pp_arg`, its stars `_gsc_stars`: `&q` of a `*G<X>`, a `**G<X>` name, field or call, one pointee
# down per star past two); a G<X> there binds X, anything else i64. It ran the base. CHANGELOG [6.7.16]
fn _gen_infer_sc(S, fi, open, f, mth): i64 {
    var k = f & 255;
    if (k <= mth) { return 0 - 8; }
